{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>On the tenth of this month they shall take.</b> It is to be taken on the tenth and slaughtered on the fourteenth. Scripture thereby teaches you that it requires inspection for four days, and therefore its taking was set four days before its slaughter." "<b>A lamb per ancestral house.</b> For one family; and if the members of the family were numerous, perhaps one lamb could suffice for all of them — therefore Scripture says, <b>a lamb per house.</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:54.021606739Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}